---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contact — Yachenyi"
  description="Contact Yachenyi about AI agents, automation, internal tools and focused software projects."
  image="/images/generated/misty-blue-coast.webp"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="eyebrow">Contact</div>
    <h1 class="page-title">Build something<br />useful.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Best fit: focused software work where AI, automation or a small custom system can remove real operational friction.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="contact-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">A useful first message</div>
      <h2>Start with the problem.</h2>
      <p>
        A short brief is enough: what currently happens, where the friction is, what already exists, and what a successful
        outcome would look like. Architecture and implementation details can come after the problem is clear.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="contact-options">
      <a class="contact-option" href="https://github.com/yachenyanyi" rel="me">
        <span><strong>GitHub</strong><small>Code, public projects and current build activity.</small></span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="contact-option" href="/projects/">
        <span><strong>Projects</strong><small>See the kind of systems currently being built.</small></span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="contact-option" href="/lab/">
        <span><strong>Lab</strong><small>Architecture notes, experiments and implementation decisions.</small></span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
